# Pin line endings so sqlx migration checksums stay stable across machines.
# A prior CRLF->LF normalization of 0001-0023 diverged from the prod DB's
# stored checksums and crashed the backend on boot (VersionMismatch). Keep
# SQL (and shell scripts) LF-only everywhere.
*.sql text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf

# LLM prompt text, embedded verbatim into the binary via `include_str!` and,
# in at least one case (relationships/predicates.rs's
# extract_relationships_prompt_allowed_list_matches_the_registry), matched
# against a hardcoded `\n`-based marker. On a Windows checkout with the
# commonly-recommended `core.autocrlf=true`, that file silently checks out
# as CRLF while the committed blob is LF — the marker search then finds
# nothing and the test panics on a prompt file nobody actually edited.
# Caught running the full workspace test suite on Windows for what looks
# like the first time; same root cause as the *.sql/*.sh rule above, one
# glob short of covering it.
backend/prompts/*.txt text eol=lf
